<title>SPAIN: Spain's Caja de Madrid cuts prime rate to 6.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Caja de Madrid cuts prime rate to 6.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Caja de Madrid said on Friday that it cut its prime rate to 6.75 percent from 7.00 percent.</p>
<p>The move follows the Bank of Spain's decision on Thursday to reduce its key money market rate to six percent from 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
